### What happens

A `<select>` bound with `[formField]` keeps its value in sync with the model by watching its options with a `MutationObserver`. The observer is set up with `characterData: true` because an `<option>` without a `value` attribute uses its text as its value. However `isRelevantSelectMutation` in `packages/forms/signals/src/directive/select.ts` only treats a mutation as relevant when nodes were added or removed. A `characterData` record never has added or removed nodes, so text changes are always ignored.

As a result, when the model value matches an option only after that option's text changes, the select stays on no selection.

### What should happen

When the text of an option changes so that it now matches the model value, the select should show that option as selected, the same as when a matching option is added.

### Minimal repro

```ts
@Component({
  imports: [FormField],
  template: `
    <select [formField]="f">
      <option>one</option>
      <option>{{ label() }}</option>
    </select>
  `,
})
class Cmp {
  f = form(signal('two'));
  label = signal('pending');
}
```

1. Render the component. `select.value` is `''` because no option matches `'two'`.
2. Run `label.set('two')` and wait for the app to be stable.
3. `select.value` is still `''`. Expected `'two'`.

### Root cause

```ts
if (mutation.type === 'childList' || mutation.type === 'characterData') {
  if (mutation.target instanceof Comment) {
    return false;
  }
  for (const node of mutation.addedNodes) { ... }
  for (const node of mutation.removedNodes) { ... }
  return false;
}
```

For a `characterData` record `addedNodes` and `removedNodes` are empty, so the function returns `false`. A text node data change on a non comment node should be treated as relevant.

