### Description

In the workbench SQL editor, the line number of a line that has (or had) a sub-query "run" marker repeats its digits after each edit. For example, line 6 shows `6666666` and line 14 shows `1414`.

<img width="862" height="306" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/628fb3d5-542f-4732-bba4-f2be79dc3974" />

To reproduce: in the workbench, write a few queries separated by blank lines so they get "run" markers, then keep typing. The numbers on the marker lines grow by one copy per edit. Lines that never had a marker are not affected.

#### Cause

`SubQueryMarker.toDOM()` in `web-console/src/views/workbench-view/flexible-query-input/sub-query-markers.ts` returns a `DocumentFragment` with two nodes, the run button and the line number text:

```ts
const fragment = document.createDocumentFragment();
fragment.append(button, String(this.lineNumber));
return fragment;
```

CodeMirror assumes one DOM node per gutter marker: when it replaces a marker, `GutterElement.setMarkers` removes only the first node (`domPos.remove()`). The run button is removed, but the old number text node stays. The `subQueries` state field rebuilds the markers on every document change, so a marker line gains one more copy of its number with each edit.

#### Suggested fix

Return a single element, so CodeMirror removes the number with the button:

```ts
const element = document.createElement('span');
element.append(button, String(this.lineNumber));
return element;
```

