{"repository": "apache/hudi", "task_candidate_id": 580, "repository_id": 17, "issue_number": 20175, "github_issue_id": 5654679589, "html_url": "https://github.com/apache/hudi/issues/20175", "created_at": "2026-10-01T00:05:31+00:00", "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR", "title": "Add an update as delete and insert operation mode for merge-on-read tables", "body_text": "A merge-on-read update appends the new version of a record to the log of its current file group. Hudi's own readers merge that correctly, but an external table format (RFC-93) whose storage model is immutable data files plus positional delete files cannot represent such a log until the next compaction. The external table format plugin therefore records merge-on-read deltacommits as empty changes, and external table format readers see stale data between compactions. Compaction and merge-on-read rollback also complete without notifying the plugin.

Proposal: a new operation mode in which an update becomes a positional delete against the record's current file group plus an insert into a new file slice, so log files carry positional deletes only and every live record stays in a base file; the external table format completion hook also fires on compaction, log compaction and merge-on-read rollback. Design in RFC-114 (number claimed in #20174); writer changes in #20167.
