{"repository": "apache/hudi", "task_candidate_id": 594, "repository_id": 17, "issue_number": 20249, "github_issue_id": 5774061656, "html_url": "https://github.com/apache/hudi/issues/20249", "created_at": "2026-10-09T06:45:37+00:00", "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR", "title": "Hudi Streamer compares the source schema with the target schema for every record", "body_text": "On the Hudi Streamer path without a transformer, `LazyCastingIterator` calls `HoodieAvroUtils.rewriteRecordDeep(record, targetSchema)` for every source record. The target schema is parsed per partition, so it is never the same instance as the record schema, and every record pays a deep Avro `Schema.equals` before being returned unchanged. On a 30-column schema that is about 0.8 us and 4.9 KB of allocation per record.

