body_text:
### Bug Description

**What happened:**

`SparkRDDWriteClient.scheduleLogCompaction(Option.empty())` fails with `NullPointerException: Expected a non-null value. Got null` in `HoodieCDCDataBlock` when a Merge-on-Read file slice contains CDC log blocks and the planner takes the block-metadata scanning path. Reproduced with the official Hudi 1.2.1 Spark 3.5 bundle, and separately with 1.1.0. No Hudi code was patched or scheduler checks bypassed.

**What you expected:**

Scheduling should inspect valid CDC log blocks without throwing. In this sparse workload no file group reaches the threshold, so it should return an empty instant, as the CDC-disabled control does, preserving snapshot/CDC semantics.

**Steps to reproduce on 1.2.1:**

1. Create a fresh MOR table, CDC enabled (`data_before_after`), partition `part`, record key `id`, ordering field `ts`. Disable automatic compaction/cleaning and metadata table.
2. Bulk-insert rows `a`,`b` into partition `p`, then update both in three separate delta commits.
3. Schedule, execute, and **commit regular compaction**. Verify a physical `.cdc` log file is generated.
4. Update `a`,`b` in `p` in three more delta commits.
5. Insert/update row `z` in partition `q` across seven separate delta commits. There are now **10 table-wide delta commits since regular compaction**, while `p` has only three subsequent data logs plus its CDC log.
6. Set `hoodie.log.compaction.blocks.threshold=10`, construct the write client with the table schema, call `scheduleLogCompaction(Option.empty())`.
7. The block metadata scanner throws the NPE below.

**Trigger detail:** 1.2.1 has a table-wide delta-commit gate. Three post-compaction commits with threshold 10 return an early no-op and mask this failure. Ten commits distributed across file groups pass that gate while requiring scanning of a sparse file group. A lower threshold can bypass the scanner through its log-file-count fast path; that does not demonstrate a fix.

**Validation:** 14 local scenarios: 3 successful log compactions, 7 clean no-ops, 4 expected scheduling NPEs. The four failures cover `data_before_after`, `data_before`, `op_key_only`, and CDC disabled in table properties after physical CDC logs were generated. The equivalent distributed CDC-disabled control returns a clean no-op. Thus existing CDC blocks are the trigger, not just the current CDC flag. Snapshot rows matched expected values before the attempt and were unchanged afterward. Full CDC query results remained unchanged where CDC stayed enabled. No data loss was observed; the demonstrated impact is failure to schedule log compaction.

The complete standalone Java reproducer, configs, case results and source analysis are included below. Its `REPRODUCTION_VERIFIED cases=14 expected_NPE=4` result means the bug was reproduced, not fixed.

**Duplicate search:** No matching open or closed report found for `HoodieCDCDataBlock`, `HoodieLogBlockMetadataScanner`, `logcompaction NullPointerException`, or `log compaction CDC`.

### Environment

**Hudi version:** 1.2.1, official `org.apache.hudi:hudi-spark3.5-bundle_2.12:1.2.1`, fresh table version 9. Also reproduced on 1.1.0; intermediate versions not runtime-tested.
**Query engine:** Spark 3.5.6, Scala 2.12, `local[2]`.
**Runtime:** OpenJDK 11.0.32.1, macOS 26.6/aarch64, local filesystem, 3 GB heap. No Docker, external catalog, Hive metastore or custom record merger.
**Relevant configs:**
```properties
hoodie.datasource.write.table.type=MERGE_ON_READ
hoodie.datasource.write.recordkey.field=id
hoodie.datasource.write.precombine.field=ts
hoodie.datasource.write.partitionpath.field=part
hoodie.table.cdc.enabled=true
hoodie.table.cdc.supplemental.logging.mode=data_before_after
hoodie.metadata.enable=false
hoodie.compact.inline=false
hoodie.compact.schedule.inline=false
hoodie.compact.inline.max.delta.commits=1
hoodie.clean.automatic=false
hoodie.archive.automatic=false
hoodie.log.compaction.enable=false
hoodie.log.compaction.blocks.threshold=10
hoodie.embed.timeline.server=false
hoodie.write.markers.type=DIRECT
```
Compaction/log compaction are explicitly invoked through the write client. Shuffle parallelism is 1; Spark uses Kryo and Hudi SQL extension/catalog. The full harness and options are included below.

The unmodified Maven Central bundle was verified against published SHA-1 `1120807b30891d6e32e4c71512b8f4fbfa2a8d50`.

### Logs and Stack Trace

```text
java.lang.NullPointerException: Expected a non-null value. Got null
  at org.apache.hudi.common.util.Option.<init>(Option.java:65)
  at org.apache.hudi.common.util.Option.of(Option.java:76)
  at org.apache.hudi.common.table.log.block.HoodieCDCDataBlock.<init>(HoodieCDCDataBlock.java:45)
  at org.apache.hudi.common.table.log.HoodieLogFileReader.readBlock(HoodieLogFileReader.java:212)
  at org.apache.hudi.common.table.log.HoodieLogFileReader.next(HoodieLogFileReader.java:379)
  at org.apache.hudi.common.table.log.HoodieLogFormatReader.next(HoodieLogFormatReader.java:100)
  at org.apache.hudi.common.table.log.BaseHoodieLogRecordReader.scanInternal(BaseHoodieLogRecordReader.java:286)
  at org.apache.hudi.common.table.log.HoodieLogBlockMetadataScanner.<init>(HoodieLogBlockMetadataScanner.java:41)
  at org.apache.hudi.table.action.compact.plan.generators.HoodieLogCompactionPlanGenerator.isFileSliceEligibleForLogCompaction(HoodieLogCompactionPlanGenerator.java:104)
  at org.apache.hudi.table.action.compact.plan.generators.HoodieLogCompactionPlanGenerator.filterFileSlice(HoodieLogCompactionPlanGenerator.java:78)
  at org.apache.hudi.table.action.compact.plan.generators.BaseHoodieCompactionPlanGenerator.lambda$generateCompactionPlan$2(BaseHoodieCompactionPlanGenerator.java:132)
```

**Root-cause analysis:** The metadata scanner creates a reader context without a schema handler. `BaseHoodieLogRecordReader` therefore has a null reader schema. `HoodieLogFileReader` passes that null into the CDC block constructor, which calls `Option.of(readerSchema)`.

Relevant 1.2.1 source:

- [Planner and file-count fast path](https://github.com/apache/hudi/blob/release-1.2.1/hudi-client/hudi-client-common/src/main/java/org/apache/hudi/table/action/compact/plan/generators/HoodieLogCompactionPlanGenerator.java)
- [Metadata scanner](https://github.com/apache/hudi/blob/release-1.2.1/hudi-common/src/main/java/org/apache/hudi/common/table/log/HoodieLogBlockMetadataScanner.java)
- [CDC block constructor](https://github.com/apache/hudi/blob/release-1.2.1/hudi-common/src/main/java/org/apache/hudi/common/table/log/block/HoodieCDCDataBlock.java)

A fix should cover both CDC-enabled tables and retained CDC logs after disabling CDC, and preserve CDC readability. A null-handling change alone should not be assumed sufficient without checking the scanner's handling of CDC block types.

**Duplicate search:** Searched open and closed upstream issues for `HoodieCDCDataBlock`, `HoodieLogBlockMetadataScanner`, `logcompaction NullPointerException`, and `log compaction CDC`; no matching report was found.

### Reproducer

The standalone harness below was compiled and run against the official 1.2.1 bundle with the Spark 3.5.6 runtime. Its assertions verify the observed bug and control outcomes; `REPRODUCTION_VERIFIED cases=14 expected_NPE=4` means the reproduction succeeded, not that the bug is fixed. The Spark application name has been generalized for this report.

Save the Java source as `CdcLogCompactionRepro.java`. With Java 11 and `REPRO_CP` containing the Spark 3.5.6 runtime dependencies plus the Hudi 1.2.1 Spark 3.5/Scala 2.12 bundle (and no older Hudi bundle):

```bash
mkdir -p evidence classes
javac -cp "$REPRO_CP" -d classes CdcLogCompactionRepro.java
SPARK_LOCAL_IP=127.0.0.1 java -Xmx3g -cp "classes:$REPRO_CP" CdcLogCompactionRepro
```

The test creates fresh disposable tables beneath `evidence/` and retains them for inspection. It does not connect to a cluster or use any private dataset.


<details>
<summary>Complete Java reproducer (14 cases)</summary>

```java
import java.nio.file.*;
import java.util.*;
import java.util.stream.*;
import org.apache.spark.sql.*;
import org.apache.spark.api.java.JavaSparkContext;
import org.apache.hudi.client.SparkRDDWriteClient;
import org.apache.hudi.client.common.HoodieSparkEngineContext;
import org.apache.hudi.common.table.HoodieTableMetaClient;
import org.apache.hudi.common.table.HoodieTableConfig;
import org.apache.hudi.common.table.TableSchemaResolver;
import org.apache.hudi.common.util.Option;
import org.apache.hudi.config.HoodieWriteConfig;
import org.apache.hudi.hadoop.fs.HadoopFSUtils;
import org.apache.hudi.table.action.HoodieWriteMetadata;

public class CdcLogCompactionRepro {
  static SparkSession spark;
  static JavaSparkContext jsc;
  static Path root;
  static int validatedCases;
  public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
    TimeZone.setDefault(TimeZone.getTimeZone("UTC"));
    root = Files.createTempDirectory(Paths.get("evidence"), "tables-").toAbsolutePath();
    System.out.println("EVIDENCE_ROOT=" + root);
    System.out.println("HUDI_RUNTIME=" + SparkRDDWriteClient.class.getProtectionDomain().getCodeSource().getLocation());
    spark = SparkSession.builder().master("local[2]").appName("hudi-cdc-logcompaction-repro")
        .config("spark.driver.host", "127.0.0.1").config("spark.driver.bindAddress", "127.0.0.1")
        .config("spark.ui.enabled", "false").config("spark.sql.shuffle.partitions", "1")
        .config("spark.default.parallelism", "1").config("spark.serializer", "org.apache.spark.serializer.KryoSerializer")
        .config("spark.sql.extensions", "org.apache.spark.sql.hudi.HoodieSparkSessionExtension")
        .config("spark.sql.catalog.spark_catalog", "org.apache.spark.sql.hudi.catalog.HoodieCatalog")
        .config("spark.sql.adaptive.enabled", "false").getOrCreate();
    spark.sparkContext().setLogLevel("ERROR");
    jsc = JavaSparkContext.fromSparkContext(spark.sparkContext());
    try {
      runCase("cdc_disabled", false, false);
      runCase("cdc_enabled_logs", true, false);
      runCase("cdc_enabled_after_compaction", true, true);
      runCase("cdc_disabled_threshold10", false, true);
      runCase("cdc_enabled_no_blocks_threshold10", true, false);
      runCase("cdc_blocks_threshold10", true, true);
      runCase("cdc_data_before_threshold10", true, true);
      runCase("cdc_op_key_only_threshold10", true, true);
      runCase("cdc_flag_disabled_existing_blocks_threshold10", true, true);
      runCase("sparse_cdc_disabled_threshold10", false, true);
      runCase("sparse_cdc_blocks_threshold10", true, true);
      runCase("sparse_cdc_data_before_threshold10", true, true);
      runCase("sparse_cdc_op_key_only_threshold10", true, true);
      runCase("sparse_cdc_flag_disabled_existing_blocks_threshold10", true, true);
      if (validatedCases != 14) throw new AssertionError("Missing results: " + validatedCases);
      System.out.println("REPRODUCTION_VERIFIED cases=" + validatedCases + " expected_NPE=4");
    } finally { spark.stop(); }
  }
  static Map<String,String> options(String name, boolean cdc) {
    Map<String,String> p = new HashMap<>();
    p.put("hoodie.table.name", name);
    p.put("hoodie.datasource.write.table.type", "MERGE_ON_READ");
    p.put("hoodie.datasource.write.recordkey.field", "id");
    p.put("hoodie.datasource.write.precombine.field", "ts");
    p.put("hoodie.datasource.write.partitionpath.field", "part");
    p.put("hoodie.table.cdc.enabled", String.valueOf(cdc));
    p.put("hoodie.table.cdc.supplemental.logging.mode", "data_before_after");
    p.put("hoodie.metadata.enable", "false");
    p.put("hoodie.compact.inline", "false");
    p.put("hoodie.compact.schedule.inline", "false");
    p.put("hoodie.compact.inline.max.delta.commits", "1");
    p.put("hoodie.clean.automatic", "false");
    p.put("hoodie.archive.automatic", "false");
    p.put("hoodie.log.compaction.enable", "false");
    p.put("hoodie.log.compaction.blocks.threshold", "3");
    p.put("hoodie.embed.timeline.server", "false");
    p.put("hoodie.write.markers.type", "DIRECT");
    p.put("hoodie.insert.shuffle.parallelism", "1");
    p.put("hoodie.upsert.shuffle.parallelism", "1");
    p.put("hoodie.bulkinsert.shuffle.parallelism", "1");
    p.put("hoodie.delete.shuffle.parallelism", "1");
    return p;
  }
  static void write(String path, Map<String,String> opts, int n) {
    Dataset<Row> df = spark.read().json(spark.createDataset(Arrays.asList(
        "{\"id\":\"a\",\"ts\":" + n + ",\"value\":\"a" + n + "\",\"part\":\"p\"}",
        "{\"id\":\"b\",\"ts\":" + n + ",\"value\":\"b" + n + "\",\"part\":\"p\"}"), Encoders.STRING()));
    df.coalesce(1).write().format("hudi").options(opts)
        .option("hoodie.datasource.write.operation", n == 0 ? "bulk_insert" : "upsert")
        .mode(SaveMode.Append).save(path);
  }
  static HoodieTableMetaClient meta(String path) {
    return HoodieTableMetaClient.builder().setConf(HadoopFSUtils.getStorageConf(jsc.hadoopConfiguration()))
        .setBasePath(path).setLoadActiveTimelineOnLoad(true).build();
  }
  static SparkRDDWriteClient client(String path, Map<String,String> opts) throws Exception {
    Properties p = new Properties(); p.putAll(opts);
    HoodieWriteConfig cfg = HoodieWriteConfig.newBuilder().withPath(path).forTable(opts.get("hoodie.table.name"))
        .withSchema(new TableSchemaResolver(meta(path)).getTableSchema().toString()).withProps(p).build();
    return new SparkRDDWriteClient(new HoodieSparkEngineContext(jsc), cfg);
  }
  static List<String> snapshot(String path) {
    return spark.read().format("hudi").load(path).select("id","ts","value","part").orderBy("id").toJSON().collectAsList();
  }
  static List<String> cdcRows(String path) {
    List<String> rows = new ArrayList<>(spark.read().format("hudi")
        .option("hoodie.datasource.query.type", "incremental")
        .option("hoodie.datasource.query.incremental.format", "cdc")
        .option("hoodie.datasource.read.begin.instanttime", "000")
        .load(path).toJSON().collectAsList());
    Collections.sort(rows);
    return rows;
  }
  static boolean hasNpe(Throwable t) {
    for (Throwable c=t;c!=null;c=c.getCause()) {
      if (c instanceof NullPointerException && c.getMessage().contains("non-null")) return true;
    }
    return false;
  }
  static void runCase(String name, boolean cdc, boolean compactFirst) throws Exception {
    System.out.println("CASE_BEGIN=" + name);
    String path = root.resolve(name).toString();
    Map<String,String> opts = options(name, cdc);
    if (name.endsWith("threshold10")) opts.put("hoodie.log.compaction.blocks.threshold", "10");
    if (name.contains("data_before_threshold")) opts.put("hoodie.table.cdc.supplemental.logging.mode", "data_before");
    if (name.contains("op_key_only")) opts.put("hoodie.table.cdc.supplemental.logging.mode", "op_key_only");
    write(path, opts, 0);
    for (int n=1;n<=3;n++) write(path, opts, n);
    if (compactFirst) {
      try (SparkRDDWriteClient c = client(path, opts)) {
        Option<String> instant = c.scheduleCompaction(Option.empty());
        if (!instant.isPresent()) throw new AssertionError("No regular compaction scheduled");
        HoodieWriteMetadata result = c.compact(instant.get());
        c.commitCompaction(instant.get(), result, Option.empty());
        System.out.println("REGULAR_COMPACTION=" + instant.get());
      }
      for (int n=4;n<=6;n++) write(path, opts, n);
    }
